  "summary": "Unpinned git dependency resolves attacker-controllable code at install",
  "details": "package.json declares the runtime dependency `libsignal` as `git+https://github.com/whiskeysockets/libsignal-node` with no commit SHA, tag, or branch pin. On `npm install`, npm clones the current HEAD of that external repository and runs any lifecycle scripts it contains, with no version pin and no integrity check. Whoever controls that repository tip controls code executed on the installer's machine. This is a third-party fork (`@silent404/baileys`) of the upstream Baileys library, so the off-registry source is not matched by the publishing scope.",
